From: BashKitten contributors
Subject: [PATCH] meson: order common compilation after its generated enum header

common/panel-utils.h includes libxfce4panel.h, which includes the generated
enum-types header. A clean parallel build can compile panel-utils before the
header exists. Declare the header as an input without linking the common
library to libxfce4panel or changing runtime behavior.

--- a/common/meson.build
+++ b/common/meson.build
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 libpanel_common = static_library(
   'panel-common',
   [
+    libpanel_enums[0],
     'panel-debug.c',
     'panel-debug.h',
     'panel-utils.c',
